# 2026-09-01 17:52:29.908298
+Read content/articles/_TEMPLATE.md.txt and content/ai-watch/2026-08-21.mdx to strictly adopt our writing style, depth, and frontmatter formatting.
+
+Generate a new MDX article file at: content/ai-watch/YYYY-MM-DD.mdx
+
+Use these details for the entry:
+- Date: YYYY-MM-DD
+- Primary Story Context: [Insert 1-2 sentence market news or topic here]
+- Stock Data:
+  - NVDA: [Close Price] ([+/-X.XX%])
+  - AMD: [Close Price] ([+/-X.XX%])
+  - AVGO: [Close Price] ([+/-X.XX%])
+
+Requirements:
+1. FRONTMATTER:
+   - title: Write a sharp headline starting with "AI Watch: " or focusing on the primary ticker/theme.
+   - summary: Exactly 2 detailed sentences summarizing the event and market impact.
+   - tags: [AI, Semiconductors, Capex, Chips] (adjust relevant tags).
+   - verdict: 3-6 words (e.g., "Capex debate intact" or "financing push, mixed tape").
+   - direction: up | down | flat
+   - tickers: Format array with symbol, close, and change.
+
+2. BODY STRUCTURE:
+   - Paragraph 1: 3-4 sentences setting up today's market action, chip performance, and broader macro context.
+   - Section "## What moved": Include a markdown table with 3 columns (| Name | Change | Note |) tracking key tickers/themes.
+   - Paragraph 2: 2-3 sentences of analytical context explaining why the market reacted this way.
+   - Section "## The number behind it": 1 deep-dive paragraph highlighting a specific financial metric, deal size, or capex figure with source grounding.
+   - Section "## What to watch": 1 forward-looking paragraph calling out upcoming earnings dates, catalyst events, or risks.
+
+3. CONSTRAINTS:
+   - Maintain a factual, professional financial journal tone (no hype, no price targets).
+   - Ensure all prices in the body and tables match the frontmatter exactly.
+   - Write directly to the target file content/ai-watch/YYYY-MM-DD.mdx.

