+content\ai-watch\2026-08-24.mdx
+
+---
+
+title: "AI Watch: Broadcom Surges on Financing Deal, NVDA Steady"
+date: "2026-08-24"
+summary: "Broadcom gained ground following analyst coverage and reports of a major AI infrastructure financing package. Traders maintained a cautious stance on Nvidia while positioning ahead of mid-week earnings."
+tags: [AI, Semiconductors, Broadcom, Nvidia, Capex]
+verdict: "financing push, mixed tape"
+direction: up
+tickers:
+
+* { symbol: "NVDA", close: "216.95", change: "-0.28%" }
+* { symbol: "AMD", close: "470.63", change: "+0.38%" }
+* { symbol: "AVGO", close: "368.88", change: "+1.30%" }
+
+---
+
+Semiconductor stocks turned in a mixed session on August 24 as investors positioned portfolios ahead of critical catalyst events later in the week. Broadcom led mega-cap chipmakers higher on fresh coverage and reports of private capital structured financing options. Meanwhile, Nvidia traded flat in low-volume trading as markets braced for its imminent quarterly results.
+
+## What moved
+
+| Name | Change | Note |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| AVGO | +1.30% | BMO initiated coverage at Outperform with a $455 target; reports surfaced of a possible ~$100B AI financing package with Apollo and Blackstone |
+| NVDA | -0.28% | Stock drifted lower in a quiet session as traders position ahead of next week's fiscal Q2 report |
+| AMD | +0.38% | Tracked broader chip sentiment with modest gain in range-bound trading |
+
+Institutional appetite remained firm for custom silicon designers as broader AI capex expectations stayed elevated. However, broad market upside remained capped by elevated options volatility and defensive hedging ahead of Tier-1 earnings reports.
+
+## The number behind it
+
+Private equity giants Apollo Global Management and Blackstone were reported to be discussing up to $100 billion in structured debt and equity vehicles. These specialized funds aim to subsidize multi-gigawatt AI data center builds and custom ASIC deployments without overloading hyperscaler balance sheets.
+
+## What to watch
+
+All eyes are turned to Nvidia's upcoming earnings release scheduled for August 26, where Wall Street will closely scrutinize datacenter revenue growth, Blackwell architecture ramp timelines, and hyperscaler capex commitment guidance.
+
+---
+
