+* { symbol: "AVGO", close: "356.74", change: "-3.29%" }
+
+---
+
+Major AI hardware names experienced light selling pressure on August 25 as pre-earnings positioning dominated equity flows. Investors pared back leveraged exposure across chipmakers following multi-week rallies across the sector. Macro treasury yield ticks also applied brief pressure on high-multiple growth stocks.
+
+## What moved
+
+| Name | Change | Note |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| NVDA | -1.80% | Shares slid ahead of after-hours earnings as options markets priced in significant implied volatility |
+| AVGO | -3.29% | Pulled back after previous session's rally as tech sector momentum slowed |
+| AMD | -1.37% | Edged down alongside peer group in broad risk-off tech rotation |
+
+Market participants cited profit-taking and hedging strategies as the main catalysts behind the sector-wide pullback. Implied volatility spikes indicated that institutional portfolios chose to lock in short-term gains rather than take unhedged earnings risk into the print.
+
+## The number behind it
+
+Options market pricing reflected an expected 8.5% move in Nvidia shares post-earnings, representing over $260 billion in market capitalization sway. The magnitude underscores Nvidia's dominant weighting in broader equity indices and macroeconomic sentiment.
+
+## What to watch
+
+Nvidia reports its Q2 fiscal 2027 financial results after the market closes on August 26. Key focal points include gross margin performance and supply chain commentary regarding TSMC advanced packaging capacity.
+
