+
+---
+
+title: "AI Watch: Nvidia Tops Estimates with $96.2B Revenue, Q2 EPS Beats"
+date: "2026-08-26"
+summary: "Nvidia delivered blowout fiscal Q2 results, generating $96.22 billion in quarterly revenue and beating top and bottom-line analyst estimates. Semiconductor equities stabilized as datacenter AI demand metrics remained strong."
+tags: [AI, Semiconductors, Nvidia, Earnings, Datacenter]
+verdict: "earnings beat, demand intact"
+direction: up
+tickers:
+
+* { symbol: "NVDA", close: "209.66", change: "-1.59%" }
+* { symbol: "AMD", close: "468.10", change: "+0.84%" }
+* { symbol: "AVGO", close: "355.59", change: "-0.32%" }
+
+---
+
+Nvidia posted another record-breaking financial performance on August 26, reporting fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of $96.22 billion. Regular session trading reflected tight consolidation before the release, with NVDA closing slightly lower before jumping in after-hours trading. Secondary AI plays such as AMD saw late-session buying support as baseline sector demand was reaffirmed.
+
+## What moved
+
+| Name | Change | Note |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| NVDA | -1.59% | Closed at $209.66 during regular hours before posting record Q2 revenue of $96.22B after market close |
+| AMD | +0.84% | Rebounded during regular hours as buyers stepped in ahead of sector earnings |
+| AVGO | -0.32% | Consolidated tightly near $355.59 as market awaited broad datacenter capex confirmation |
+
+Analytical commentary highlighted surging compute requirements from cloud hyperscalers and sovereign nation infrastructure programs as key structural tailwinds. The beat alleviated short-term concerns around customer capex digestion or slowing deployment velocity.
+
+## The number behind it
+
+Nvidia reported adjusted EPS of $2.22 versus consensus estimates of $2.09, while quarterly revenue grew 105.9% year-over-year to hit $96.22 billion (surpassing $92.27 billion estimates). Datacenter segment revenue drove the vast majority of top-line expansion.
+
+## What to watch
+
+Post-earnings conference call detail regarding Q3 revenue guidance (projected at ~$103.5B) and Blackwell chip shipment volume trajectories will dictate market trajectory for the remainder of Q3.
+
+---
