+
+---
+
+AI chip stocks logged sweeping gains across Thursday's trading session as Wall Street digested Nvidia's strong earnings commentary and elevated forward guidance. Nvidia surged nearly 9% to touch $227.98, lifting the entire PHLX Semiconductor Index. Broadcom and AMD both registered multi-percentage gains as institutional inflows returned to the space.
+
+## What moved
+
+| Name | Change | Note |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| NVDA | +8.74% | Rallied aggressively to $227.98 post-earnings as guidance outpaced top-end Street estimates |
+| AVGO | +3.71% | Surged to $368.79 as custom ASIC demand and networking interconnect trends gained momentum |
+| AMD | +3.08% | Rose sharply as broader AI hardware ecosystem re-rated higher |
+
+Reassurance from tech executives regarding structural Return on Investment (ROI) from enterprise AI deployments restored confidence across equity markets. Short-covering combined with active systematic fund buying created significant tailwinds throughout the trading day.
+
+## The number behind it
+
+Nvidia's full-year fiscal 2027 revenue guidance implicit run-rate points toward multi-billion dollar capex plans across Microsoft, Alphabet, Meta, and Amazon. Consolidated datacenter spend across the top four cloud providers is now projected to top $230 billion annually.
+
+## What to watch
+
+Traders will monitor macro economic data releases and upcoming central bank policy commentary to see if technology momentum can withstand broader market valuation tests into month-end.
+
+---
